description: "Iteratively fix Rust compiler errors one at a time"
globs: ["**/*.rs"]
alwaysApply: false
---

When writing Rust:

- Write code with fully unqualified types. e.g. instead of `crate::crypto::verify_signature`, write `verify_signature` and `use` the crypto.
- Prefer being explicit for field definitions. Never use `..Default::default()`, always fill out the missing/empty fields with their defaults explicitly.
- Prefer functions over structs with implementations.